WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.798 --> 00:00:18.801
seemed as if the children had been standing next to the tracks for hours, holding their little flannel

2
00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:24.404
flags. They had to warn the train to stop before it came around the bend and crashed into

3
00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:25.425
the rocks and trees!

4
00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:34.710
Peter's watch is wrong, and the train has already gone by," said Phyllis impatiently.

5
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.071
But at last came a distant hum and a puff of white steam.

6
00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:41.372
"Wave your flags!"

7
00:00:41.772 --> 00:00:42.413
Peter shouted.

8
00:00:42.433 --> 00:00:45.874
"And Bobbie, don't stand on the tracks!"

9
00:00:47.635 --> 00:00:50.636
The train came rattling along, very, very fast.

10
00:00:50.656 --> 00:00:52.517
"They don't see us!

11
00:00:53.597 --> 00:00:54.377
It's no good!"

12
00:00:54.718 --> 00:00:55.358
cried Bobbie.

13
00:00:56.999 --> 00:01:00.360
The two flags sitting on the tracks swayed as the train approached.

14
00:01:01.472 --> 00:01:03.694
Then one tipped forward and fell onto the tracks.

15
00:01:05.795 --> 00:01:08.257
Bobbie jumped forward, and caught the flag, and waved it.

16
00:01:09.298 --> 00:01:10.879
The train came as fast as ever.

17
00:01:11.919 --> 00:01:13.020
It was very close now.

18
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.762
"Keep off the tracks, Bobbie!"

19
00:01:16.102 --> 00:01:16.843
Peter warned her.

20
00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:19.985
"It's no good," said Bobbie again.

21
00:01:20.005 --> 00:01:22.767
"Stand back, Bobbie!"

22
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:23.888
shouted Phyllis.

23
00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:27.870
But Bobbie cried, "Not yet, not yet!"

24
00:01:28.331 --> 00:01:29.752
and stood right on the tracks.

25
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.201
She waved her two flags.

26
00:01:33.281 --> 00:01:35.582
The front of the engine looked black and very big.

27
00:01:35.602 --> 00:01:38.643
"Oh, stop, stop, stop!"

28
00:01:39.043 --> 00:01:39.704
cried Bobbie.

29
00:01:40.824 --> 00:01:41.725
But no one heard her.

30
00:01:43.365 --> 00:01:46.346
Peter and Phyllis didn't hear Bobbie because of the noise of the train.

31
00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:53.349
But afterward Bobbie wondered if the engine had heard her because it slowed down quickly and stopped twenty

32
00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:54.530
meters in front of Bobbie.

33
00:01:57.331 --> 00:02:02.026
Bobbie saw the great black engine stop, but she could not stop waving the flags.

34
00:02:03.087 --> 00:02:05.769
The engine driver and the fireman jumped off the train.

35
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.311
Peter and Phyllis ran to meet them.

36
00:02:09.412 --> 00:02:12.054
Bobbie couldn't move because her legs were shaking too much.

37
00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:18.279
When the others came back to get Bobbie, she was lying on the ground, still gripping the little

38
00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:19.400
red flannel flags.

39
00:02:20.581 --> 00:02:21.242
She had fainted.

40
00:02:22.162 --> 00:02:23.584
The engine driver picked her up.

41
00:02:24.584 --> 00:02:28.588
He carried her into a first-class car, where he laid her down on some cushions.

42
00:02:31.212 --> 00:02:35.434
"I think that's what people look like when they're dead," Phyllis whispered.

43
00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.335
"Don't say that!"

44
00:02:37.835 --> 00:02:38.855
said Peter sharply.

45
00:02:39.876 --> 00:02:42.217
The train started up again and went back to the station.

46
00:02:45.258 --> 00:02:47.239
Soon Bobbie sighed and opened her eyes.

47
00:02:48.379 --> 00:02:50.300
Then she rolled over and began to cry.

48
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.662
This cheered up Peter and Phyllis because they had seen her cry before.

49
00:02:55.682 --> 00:02:57.223
But they had never seen her faint.

50
00:02:58.623 --> 00:03:03.870
When the train reached the station, a small crowd of people greeted Bobbie, Peter, and Phyllis as heroes.

51
00:03:05.291 --> 00:03:07.892
The children were praised for their bravery and quick thinking.

52
00:03:07.912 --> 00:03:11.834
"You're brave and clever children," the driver told them.

53
00:03:12.915 --> 00:03:14.196
Phyllis enjoyed the attention.

54
00:03:15.336 --> 00:03:17.157
She had never been a heroine before.

55
00:03:18.458 --> 00:03:21.039
Peter's ears got very red, but he was happy.

56
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.301
Only Bobbie wished they could all leave at that moment.

57
00:03:24.321 --> 00:03:29.344
"You'll hear from the train company about this, I expect," the stationmaster said.

58
00:03:30.496 --> 00:03:32.557
Bobbie wished she would never hear of it again.

59
00:03:33.738 --> 00:03:35.078
She pulled at Peter's jacket.

60
00:03:35.098 --> 00:03:37.219
"Come on!

61
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.720
I want to go home!"

62
00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:39.701
Bobbie said.

63
00:03:40.721 --> 00:03:43.002
She kept thinking about the pile of rocks on the track.

64
00:03:44.103 --> 00:03:46.304
What would have happened had the train crashed into it?

65
00:03:47.284 --> 00:03:48.245
And so they went home.

66
00:03:49.345 --> 00:03:54.388
As the children left the station, the stationmaster, guards, and drivers cheered.
